    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1553">

                <pb facs="0994" n="878" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg878"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.51/80.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Special Agent Canova to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Zacatecas</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-02T21:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 2, 1914, 9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Many atrocities have been committed here by the Constitutionalists. Three
                    Christian Brothers, the President, Adrien Astruc, Professor Adolphus Giles, both
                    of them French, and Father Vega, Mexican, shot June 24, 4 p.m. by order of
                    General Chao. Fourteen others banished, and now at Santa Fe, New Mexico, having
                    been forced to make a payment of $5,000 ransom. By order of the same General, 22
                    priests Zacatecas threatened death unless they paid $100,000; and upon payment
                    they were arrested and banished, were sent to El Paso. Constitutionalists’
                    conduct here deplorable because of multiplicity of crimes.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canova</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
